{
  "_doc": "The CC0 material library (UPDATE_05 section 1, T-088; docs/ART_BIBLE.md section 3). MaterialLibrary.get_mat(key) builds one shared ShaderMaterial (assets/materials/shaders/surface_pbr.gdshader) per key from `library` and caches it. set = assets/third_party/<set>/textures/<id>_{albedo,normal,orm[,height]}.png; tile_m = metres one tile covers (uv_scale = 1 / tile_m, per axis when `tile_xyz` is given); tint multiplies the albedo; rough = [min, max] clamp on the ORM's roughness; grime / wetness / frost are the shared wear parameters (0..1); frost_height = world y the frost starts above (-1000 = everywhere); triplanar false = the mesh's own UVs (props). `generator` maps the procedural Mats keys (gravelight/world/materials.gd, what gen_map0N.gd and Props call) to library keys: Mats.get_mat() hands out the library material for a key in `enabled` while use_library is true, so the environment builder switches Map 0 over one key at a time by adding to `enabled` and re-running gen_map00. Note for consumers that cast Mats.get_mat() to StandardMaterial3D (landscape.gd reads the snow's albedo_texture): a library material is a ShaderMaterial; read MaterialLibrary.texture(key, 'albedo') instead. UPDATE 19 (T-252): macro_var / macro_scale (a slow world-space brightness drift, on every triplanar surface; default 0.18 over 7 m), detile (0..1: a second, 2.7x larger sample blended in patches and with distance, for unstructured ground and render; never on coursed stone, brick or boards) and sparkle (snow glints a light sets off) are surface_pbr's variation uniforms; MaterialLibrary.build writes them and LookMaterials.apply_library (MapRoot._ready) gives them to a scene baked before they existed (by the material's lib_<key> name, else `by_texture`). `live`: true on a key whose set or look changed after the scenes were baked: its whole entry, textures included, is written to the baked material at load, so the map needs no regeneration. A tint may exceed 1 (asphalt_snow is a grey photograph).",
